--TEST--
`purge` names a queue and a filter where `delete` names one job, so the two removal members are told apart by their subject — `rule:concurrency/queue-deletion-is-explicit-and-bounded`, `rule:concurrency/queue-four-members`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The pair is one subject each: a receipt names the row and the queue it is
// in, and a queue name with a filter names a population. That is the same
// division `status` and `stats` already make, and it is why there is no
// `deleteMany` — the scale is what the filter says, not what the name does.
var $receipt = Core\Queue::push("jobs/send-receipt.nvs");
bool $one = Core\Queue::delete($receipt);
uint $many = Core\Queue::purge("email", {tag: "nightly"});

// So a receipt is not a subject this member has, even though the queue it
// carries is the name the grant would be matched against: that name arrives
// here as the argument the program wrote.
uint $wrong = Core\Queue::purge($receipt);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `Core\Queue\Id`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
